  "_comment": "CANONICAL. The scenario ROWS — what each CDM row draws in each game state — as data. This is hand-edited and it leads; `scenarios.md` beside it carries the walk prose and is keyed by the same ids. It replaced a REVIEWED CACHE under previews/data/, which ran the other way round: the doc led and the JSON was imported from it by a regex over prose. `capart check` cross-references the two by id in BOTH directions, so a walk with no row and a row with no walk are each a named failure. ⚠ Four names here are DEMON-FORM overrides — Abyssal Gaze, Death Sweep, Consuming Fire, Annihilation — and they are correct as written: a row writes whichever face the client would be showing, and `load_roster` keys every override name in catalog.md's roster table back to the same ability, so they join the state table normally.",
